@page
@model SignInModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Sign in";
}

<h1>Sign in</h1>

<p class="lead">
    This ward is invented, so the sign-in is too. What is <em>not</em> invented is
    what happens afterwards: every page can only ask the archive about the
    patient you pick, because the archive has no method that will answer without
    being told who is asking.
</p>

@if (Model.Said is not null)
{
    <p class="said">@Model.Said</p>
}

@*
    One click each, and each says what it will show.

    The password goes into the form rather than into a sentence under it. It is
    `ward`, it is in the README, it is in the source, and the page says the whole
    ward is invented — a password nobody can use on anything is not a credential,
    and making somebody type it teaches them nothing about the part of this that
    is real. The first person to open this submitted the form empty and asked
    what the credentials were, with the answer three inches below the button.
*@
<section class="pick">
    <h2>Sign in as one of them</h2>
    <p>Each shows something different. The interesting one is whoever has a document that needs a code.</p>

    <form method="post">
        <input type="hidden" name="password" value="@SignInModel.ThePassword" />

        <ul class="whom">
            @foreach (var one in Model.Choices)
            {
                <li>
                    <button type="submit" name="Patient" value="@one.Who">
                        <span class="who">@one.Who</span>

                        @* The same three colours the documents themselves use. *@
                        <span class="has">
                            @if (one.Empty)
                            {
                                <span class="none">nothing yet — the empty page</span>
                            }
                            @if (one.Readable > 0)
                            {
                                <span class="tag read"><i></i>@one.Readable to read</span>
                            }
                            @if (one.Guarded > 0)
                            {
                                <span class="tag guarded"><i></i>@one.Guarded needs a code</span>
                            }
                            @if (one.Waiting > 0)
                            {
                                <span class="tag waiting"><i></i>@one.Waiting not signed off</span>
                            }
                        </span>

                        <span class="go">Open their file</span>
                    </button>
                </li>
            }
        </ul>
    </form>
</section>

<details class="byhand">
    <summary>Or type it</summary>

    <form class="stack" method="post">
        <label>
            Patient
            <select name="Patient" asp-for="Patient">
                @foreach (var one in Model.Everyone)
                {
                    <option value="@one">@one</option>
                }
            </select>
        </label>

        <label>
            Password
            <input type="password" name="password" autocomplete="current-password" />
        </label>

        <button type="submit">Sign in</button>
    </form>

    <p class="lead">The password for every invented patient is <code>@SignInModel.ThePassword</code>.</p>
</details>
